{% comment %}
  Nourishment explorer: pick a fill; a headline, one bar per year after it (how far the shoreline sat seaward of where
  it was the year before, compared with the rest of the island), and a card. The whole record for the stretch is in a
  Go deeper box, as the stretch against the rest of the island or their difference. Observed only.
  Data from tools/hatteras_nourishment_data.py; script assets/hatteras/js/nourishment-explorer.js.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="hat-mvo hat-nx hat-bleed" data-src="{{ '/assets/hatteras/data/nourishment.json' | relative_url }}">
  <div class="hat-shoremap-inner">
    <div class="hat-controls">
      <div class="hat-seg hat-nx-stretches" role="group" aria-label="Beach fill"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hat-nx-strip"></div>
    <p class="hat-nx-headline" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div class="hat-nx-simple">
      <div class="hat-nx-bars"></div>
      <div class="hat-nx-cards"></div>
    </div>
    <p class="hat-caption hat-numbered">
      Each bar is how far the shoreline on the nourished stretch sat seaward of where it was the year before the fill,
      compared with the rest of the island, from the yearly average of every satellite shoreline. Comparing with the rest of
      the island takes out storms and island-wide shifts such as 2021, which move both. Paler bars start in the year of a later fill on
      the same stretch, so they include its sand too.
    </p>
    <details class="hat-deeper hat-nx-more">
      <summary>Go deeper: the whole record for <span class="hat-nx-stretch-name"></span>, 1984–2025</summary>
      <div class="hat-controls">
        <div class="hat-seg hat-nx-views" role="group" aria-label="What to show">
          <button type="button" data-view="relative" class="on">Relative to the rest of the island</button>
          <button type="button" data-view="raw">Shoreline position</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hat-tl-chart hat-nx-chart" role="img" aria-label="Shoreline position through time on the nourished stretch"></div>
      <div class="hat-tl-tip" role="status" hidden></div>
      <p class="hat-caption" data-for-view="relative">
        The stretch minus the rest of the island, both zero in the year before the first fill (open circle). A fill shows up
        as a jump (gold bracket: the year before to the year after). Before any fill, a falling line means the stretch was
        eroding faster than the island as a whole.
      </p>
      <p class="hat-caption" data-for-view="raw" hidden>
        The yearly average shoreline on the nourished stretch (blue) and on the rest of the island from Cape Point to Oregon Inlet (grey),
        both zero in the year before the first fill (open circle). The gap between them is the other view.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</div>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/hatteras/js/nourishment-explorer.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
